---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { CONTACT, CONTROLLER, POLICY_DATE } from "../consts";
---

<Base
  title="Contact and grievances"
  description="How to reach DynShift, and how privacy requests and grievances are handled, including under India's DPDP Act and IT Rules."
>
  <section class="wrap prose">
    <h1>Contact and grievances</h1>
    <p class="muted small">Last updated {POLICY_DATE}.</p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Everything, including privacy: <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT}`}>{CONTACT}</a>.
      For a bug or a question about a specific project, its GitHub repository
      is usually faster.
    </p>

    <h2>Grievance Officer</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>Grievance Officer, {CONTROLLER}</strong><br />
      Email: <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT}?subject=Grievance`}>{CONTACT}</a><br />
      Based in India.
    </p>
    <p>
      The Grievance Officer handles complaints and requests about personal
      data on all DynShift sites (dynshift.com, phonepad.dynshift.com and
      layr.dynshift.com): access, correction, erasure, withdrawal of consent,
      nomination, and anything else about how your data is handled.
    </p>

    <h2>How a request is handled</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>
        Write to the address above. Say which site it concerns and what you
        want done. If it is about analytics, include your Google Analytics
        client identifier if you have it; nothing else identifies you there.
      </li>
      <li>You get an acknowledgement, and a full answer within <strong>30 days</strong>.</li>
      <li>
        DynShift may ask for just enough to confirm the request is yours. It
        will never ask for a password or an identity document for this.
      </li>
      <li>
        If you are not satisfied: in India, you may complain to the Data
        Protection Board of India after this grievance process; in the EEA, the
        UK or Switzerland, to your data protection authority.
      </li>
    </ol>
    <p>
      Requests about Google's advertising data are Google's to answer, through
      <a href="https://myadcenter.google.com/" rel="noopener">My Ad Center</a> and
      Google's own privacy tools. DynShift will point you to the right place.
    </p>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  section {
    padding-block: clamp(24px, 5vw, 56px);
  }
  ol li {
    color: var(--ink2);
    margin-bottom: 0.5em;
  }
</style>
